Z||000024||DaRkLoRD||08-28-2001||11:58 AM||||defying the laws of physics.....as we understand them.<P>in the last 2 years, light has been slowed down to 38mph, and in a later experiment, stopped completely, and sped up again. A german experiment in the early 90s demonstrated a signal transmitted at approx 300x light speed. <P>I think it's unreasonable to assume that humans, who have only been "modern" for the last 100 years or so, understand everything there is to know about how reality works.. even NASA is working on technology similar to the "warp drives" of science fiction stories.. (do a search for miguel alcubierre.. probably spelled wrong..)<P>back in the early 80s, Alan C. Holt, at the Lyndon Johnson space center, was working on a "theoretical" spaceship design that used some sort of particle laser (maser?) to modulate a magnetic field around a disc-shaped craft, to create almost like a wormhole which would transport the craft to another set of spatial coordinates.. the design of this sound suspiciously like the "flying saucers" which have been spotted many times over the last few decades... HMM..     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>(this is called Field Resonance Propulsion) <A HREF="http://www.keelynet.com/energy/holt1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.keelynet.com/energy/holt1.htm</A>  <A HREF="http://www.keelynet.com/energy/holt2.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.keelynet.com/energy/holt2.htm</A> <P><BR>anyway, as for the craft I saw.. yes, it might have been the Aurora, though it wasn't loud enough for the engine that the Aurora supposedly has. (pulse detonation wave engine) I used to correspond with several engineers at Lockheed, including the engineer that was in charge of testing the X-36 drone at white sands.. I also used to email a scientist who was developing the next generation of PDWEs... I made a few suggestions to her and her colleagues, but they'd already thought of everything I said.. not surprising, since I was only 17 at the time..<P>I have seen the contrail from a pulsejet before, but not a pulse detonation wave engine.. they're very distinctive, a thin contrail with smoke rings surrounding it, spaced at regular intervals. it;s known as a "donuts on a rope trail".. very apt description.<P>just a side note, Ben Rich, former head of Lockheed Martin Skunk Works, on his deathbed allegedly said that humans have interstellar spacecraft technology.. there's no reason for him to lie about this, and he wasn't reported to be delusional.. he didn't say where they got the tech though... it might be derived from recovered alien tech, or it might be a spinoff from previous military experiments involving spacetime modification (philadelphia experiment etc)<P>either way.. I'm inclined to believe it's true.<P>------------------<BR>       <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 08-28-2001).]||||reg||3
