Z||000029||Ken Wittlief||08-28-2001||01:41 PM||||we've only been modern for the last 100 years?!<P>at any given point in history we were always 'modern'.<P>people knew the earth was spherical, and had a pretty close estimate to how large it was thousands of years before Columbus sailed, based on the angle the sun makes at differnt lattitudes at noon.<P>we know that teenagers always think they are smarter than their parents cause 'everything has changed since you were a kid - dad!' this has been true for the last 6000 years.<P>but we are also guilty of the same arrogant assumption as adults - we think we are light years ahead of our ansestors - we know almost everything and they were all oafs.<P>because technology builds on the work that went before it, yes we do have a collective knowledge of science that is at its highest point in the last few thousand years, at least that we know of<P>but genetics shows us that intellectually we degrade over the generations, we get dumber and dumber.<P>so even though modern medicine keeps us in better health, and we live longer now, its most likely that we are less intelligent than our ancestors were - so if you go back several thousand years its possible the average person was a genius by our modern standards.<P> so whats my point? whether its by blind faith that we dont understand everything about science yet, or by blind faith that we dont understand hardly anything about spiritual beings, in either case, this kinda stuff has been happening to humans for several thousand years<P>its arrogant to take the stance that we understand it correctly now, and that the millions of those who have preceeded us were a bunch of superstitious backwards caveman like dolts.<P>and since it has been going on for thousands of years, and in the past these beings have been deceptive, conniving, and misrepresented themselves to manipulate us to serve their purposes, why should we now assume they are not still doing the same old thing?||||reg||1
Z||000030||DaRkLoRD||08-28-2001||01:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>we've only been modern for the last 100 years?!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was referring to the industrial revolution, mostly.. and if I thought our ancient ancestors were cavemen like dolts, etc... how could they have built the great pyramid at giza, which would be almost impossible to copy now, even with all our technology?<BR>but that's a whole new topic.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>p.s. I fully agree that some of the unexplained sightings could be spiritual or other paranormal phenomenon.. and some are hoaxes.. and some are hallucinations.. but I believe that some are classified military tech, and some are alien craft... but so far I haven't seen anything pesonally to suspect what I have seen was alien or otherwise paranormal.. everything I've seen, I can grasp the concepts of operation of, so it's easily explainable as human technology.<P>but, again, I don't discount other explanations, simply because I haven't witnessd the phenomenon myself.<P>(regarding other spiritual/paranormal events... I've seen some stuff that cannot be explained by anything other than the paranormal.)<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
