Z||000088||Fierowrecker||08-29-2001||10:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>How's everybody doin on their beers?  Do we need another round here at our table?  I'm buying this round?  Ken?  DRH?  starfighter? lou_dias?  Anybody else need a refill while I'm at it?  The rest of you fine?<P>Waitress!  Waitress!  Another round for the boys and I!<P>Anywhooo, sorry I was gone so long.  Good thing these converstations are recorded though, especially where I last left off.<P>As far as believing what we want to believe and looking for facts to support it, the same argument can be made   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> &lt;dawns extra heavy duty flame suite just in case&gt; about the exsistance of a God.  I'm not attempting to turn this into a religous arguement.<P>Hope you have your Nomex undies on!<P><BR>What actual support is there of his exsistance, other then passages in the bibles, stories handed down from generation to generation and the belief that a God exsisted?  When has he actually "physically" appeared to someone with credibility?  How do we in fact know for 100% certantity that God does in fact exsist and that he had a son called Jesus?<P>Early man was taught religion by God himself, later he sent his Son to continue the teaching. Today, we take the word of God in faith.<P>Our genetic makeup in the atmosphere we live in:  Well, if it takes DNA/RNA and our atmosphere to exsist as an intelligent species, then how is this supposed God living?  I don't see him anywhere here. Havent seen him on a cloud waiving when I've been flowin over, so he must be living in some other medium, perhaps space.  But of course, that does not have oxygen.  Okay.  So perhaps he is energy.  Well then DNA/RNA and the like can be thrown out needed as an argument to support life as well.<P>God does not have a body as you or I, nor does he flit around checking up on every one. He exsists everywhere at all times.<P>Complexity of life:  What is to say life is actually easier then what we take it for. But we just have not come to a stage in our development to recognize or see it.<P>Man has tried may times to duplicate the accidental occurance of life, but have failed every time. That is why "seeding" has become a popular subject with science.<BR>Look at the "mars rock", it shows signs of life, or so they claim... But it is their icon of faith that seeding might work!<P>As far as SETI listening, perhaps yes, this is a waste of time, because of two theories that could exsist 1) A race is not technologically advanced 2) a race is technologically advanced but does not use that which we seek.  They could also be out there listening for planets like us and might not be hearing us because they are listening for the wrong thing.<P>Good point! They are listening, but not transmitting, We are listening and not transmitting, lots of good communication?<P>And if we are or do come to the point where we can spread the seeds of life to other galaxies, are we not becoming a GOD ourselves?<P>No, we would be farmers...<P>Who is to say that we are just one huge experiment in a gigantic petri dish called Earth?  And the so called visitors and reported abductions are nothing more then space alien scientist checking the results much like our scientists in a lab do.  We are just the organism being studied.<P>Or deluded people trying to justify their exsistance without God?<P>Now if we look back in our own history, it has been found/discovered that in many of our civilizations documents, drawing and paintings, going right back to cave man time of them making notations either pictorially or written of strange objects in the air.  Pre historic cave drawings which were verified as authentic due to the pigments make up that they used during that time, had dipicted objects that had represented many of today's sightings, including that of something that looked like an airplane.<P>Okay, maybe it is only a couple hundred years old.  However, it still shows something far more advanced.<P>How many people report UFO's when it is natural phenomina...<P>Japanese as well as Chinese dipictions from the 15th through 18th century also have had depictions of UFO like crafts with technologically advanced lights and other things that were not even invented yet.<P>Yet the chinese had kites big enough to carry a man into the air...<P>Many earlier tribes and civilizations had built runways and large depictions of alien like creatures, including that of an airplane years and years before the plane was developed.<P>Look closely at those desert drawings again, the pictographs are of animals that are highly stylized... And the runways are roads that travel to hills and mesas, not good for aircraft to take off or land on...<P>We subsequently can neither prove nor can we disprove the exsistance of God with a 100% certaintity other then faith and/or hope.<P>I have to take it on faith that Rome and Egypt went along with the early Christians in creating a new false religion then?<BR>Jesus is in their records...<P>We subsequently can neither prove nor can we disprove the exsistance of other life on other planets with a 100% certaintity, once again other then faith and/or hope.<P>I am a Christian and I would gladly welcome people from another planet. It does not destroy my belief in God if other planets have life...<P>Are you wrong?  No<BR>Am I wrong? No<BR>Is the people all around you wrong? No<P>That is why we have the YING/YANG of life.  It opens us all up to possibilities.  And as we know, everything has an opposite as well as plausible side.<P>Either that, or we are getting drunk sitting here talking about this and in all actuality, basically we have and/or are saying the same thing.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Where are those beers that I ordered for us.  We need to wet our whistles you know!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
