Z||000091||Mach10||08-30-2001||02:28 AM||||Ken: I would disagree there. The basic elements of life are VERY simple. I will concede that the DNA structure that currently makes up our existence is maddeningly complex. But what it boils down to (literally) is that life seems to be a large number of simple organic reactions. Carbon is very abundant in the universe, as is Oxygen, Nitrogen, and Hydrogen. That's pretty much all you need (leaving out a couple of important trace elements) The conditions in which these compounds react are fairly easy to reproduce (i.e., common).<P>NOW, the main question is, how does one define life? Let's say for agument that "life" consists of having a defined boundary (i.e., cell wall, membrane, skin, whatever), transforms energy (consumer, photo-producer, thermal), and creates replicas of itself(doin' the nasty, or fission).<BR>You don't NEED DNA to do this. I'm reasonably sure that there are plenty of ways of getting around this without Ribonucleic acids. Other sugars will do, in a pinch. What if DNA's the hard way? To be fair, the chances of extra-terrestrial life being anything like ours is remote. But it's pretty arrogant for a species to believe that ours is the only way of going about it. Look at the little buggers hanging around volcanic vents, kilometers beneath the seas, in places where --until recently-- we were positive that life could not possibly exist...<P>If one sticks to the aforementioned guidelines, I'd have to say that life is pretty abundant. Now, the problem with complex lifeforms, is that you need a space where conditions remain within a certain boundary for billions of years. Time to evolve and stuff. This, of course is the tricky bit. It's no good hunting for ET, if it turns out that our planet is the only one that stays reasonably constant (with respect to life-supporting environmental conditions). If this is the case, then the only thing we will find is many, many planets populated entirely with primal ooze, and single-celled microbes. Then of course, the sun will set, everything will die, and have to be re-created in the next 1000 years when it rises again.<P>So yes, I firmly believe that we aren't alone. However, I'm not so hopeful about meeting one. There's only so much conversation that can be had using only two words: Stimulus, Response.<P>SETI is a great idea, assuming that someone IS trying to communicate. This is most likely not the case. However, if there is a lottery-type chance that someone is, I'd rather have at least a few people keeping an ear open... If nothing else, it beats turning off your computer everynight. Besides, it's a nifty screensaver  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000092||lou_dias||08-30-2001||10:00 AM||||California Kid - u da man!<BR>I read about all that stuff like 13 years ago.  The only change I would make is don't do anything fun today that may bite you in the arse tomorrow and from then on.<P>do you know about one of the moons on Jupiter or Saturn that contains alot of water(ice) that recently had some activity (3-months to a year ago) that is supposed to be the new home for mankind once that geological disaster takes place.  I read about this 12+ years ago and then seeing that on the news was like whoa...<P>After a while you can tell what is disinformation and what is fact because the factual stuff eventual unfolds and presents itself.<P>Anybody see how complex crop circles are getting?  Impossible that they are man-made by a small group of people.  they are too big, to complex and too perfect.  I think it's a way of establishing communications.  Eventually there will be a video of a ufo creating these if it doesn't get snuffed out by the government first.<P>The only way to safely distribute such a video is to copy it and send it to every news agency at the same time and have them all air it withou prior announcement.  Remember, our government can declare Marshall law at anytime and take over all media.  It's sad that a goverment founded to give power to the people has mutated into on that takes it away "for our own good".  Thanks BIG BROTHER...<P>At one time I read that we are in a state of Marshall Law already so that it doesn't have to bother declaring it and can do what it wants.<P>Ever wonder why the Reform Party and other independants never get to debate on the major networks?  What if one of them actually got elected instead of the polical lackeys we've always had?||||reg||1
