Z||000094||rogergarrison||08-30-2001||11:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lou_dias:<BR><B><P>Anybody see how complex crop circles are getting?  Impossible that they are man-made by a small group of people.  they are too big, to complex and too perfect.  I think it's a way of establishing communications.  Eventually there will be a video of a ufo creating these if it doesn't get snuffed out by the government first.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>There is a video. A guy driving in England saw two English military helicopters with no markings on them circling a field and got out with a video camera to tape them. It was then that he saw them trying to corner a ball of light flying around and creating a crop circle while he watched. One helicopter stopped in the air face to face with it for a few seconds while the other buzzed the guy trying to scare him off. the light blasted off and the 2 copters tried to follow. It was in one of the UFO documentaries during the spring. In the video you could clearly see the whole thing.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000095||Ken Wittlief||08-30-2001||12:18 PM||||oh boy - so many responses - lets see if I can remember everything.<P>cant prove the existance of God?! sure you can. God comes to your house, knocks on your door, and introduces himself. God would have to reveal Himself. Whats so hard about that?<P>cant prove the existance of life on other planets? Sure you can. You go to one, you find life there, you cant account for anyway life could of gotten from here to there - bingo: alien life!<P>Ying Yang?! thats a religious concept that good and evil are in balance and both are necessary, and that one is really not morally any better than the other.<P>Am I off the subject?! arnt we talking about UFOs?! Facts?! the science of biology and astromny are facts. If you want to bury your head in the sand and ignore them, thats your choice.<P>Life is made of simple elements?! If I remember right DNA is made of 4 proteins. But those protiens are not simply carbon, hydrogen.... they are extreemly complex - they have to be exactly right - if you throw the elements together what you almost always get is a tar like substance - toxic!<P>that is what I am talking about with the odds against life happening - if the LIFE game were a lottery and if every atom in the UNIVERSE has been playing it, once every SECOND since the big bang, then according to the odds, simple proteins that make up life should not have been created yet, not even one strand, not even once, ANYWHERE!<P>Get the point? if the odds of winning the lottery are a million to one, and so far only ten people have played, ten times each, then they havent even scratched the surface for all the possible combinations, and statistics predict no one will win until about half the 1 million combinations have been played, and that is assuming the players are keeping track and are playing a diffent combination each time, not playing at random.<P>for the assumptions used in Drakes equation to be correct, it would be the same as if every time EVERYONE goes out and buys their first powerball ticket, they WIN! Not gonna happen!<P>We have been suckered down that path. When the idea of evolution was first proposed they said a one cell life form could spring into existance easily if the right chemicals are present - how hard can it be - its only one CELL!!! there are only a few elements involved.<P> but when we learned about DNA, and protein strands, thats when they realized the complexity of a one celled organism is on the order of 10E380 - there are that many possible combinations and if you get it wrong, its not viable and it dies.<P>A fact finding mission is great - you can take two approaches - you can go back and study an event that happened 53 years ago, and read the accounts, and look for 'evidence'... But in the end, what difference does it make? seriously!<P>If aliens came here 53 years ago and crashed, then so what? What now? Are they coming back? Can a dead alien explain why he was here? Can we do anything but reverse engineer their technology, maybe?<P>I think the more important question is what are the aliens doing THIS WEEK? Where are they now? what are they up to? are they coming back? Do they exist at all?<P>It comes down to this, are we gonna scratch around in the desert looking for pieces of a crashed ufo to convince ourselves that something interesting happened 53 years ago? Are we gonna point antennas at the sky and hope someone sends us a profound message? Are we gonna put landing lights in the desert and hope a flying saucer sees em and lands?<P> or are we gonna take the other approach? are we gonna get off our butts and do something proactive? are we gonna take interstellar travel seriously and start working on it?<P>  are we gonna sit around and wait for them to come to us? Or are we going to grasp our current situation and technology, take what we have now, and get on with fullfilling our destiny?<P>and BTW: art bell is entertainment, like tabloids, professional wrestling, and football games - if you want to be entertained then tune in - if you want to learn something useful, study Physics.||||reg||10
