Z||000101||Mach10||08-30-2001||05:39 PM||||Ken: DNA is made up of 5(6 for RNA copies) parts:<BR>Deoxyribose sugar(acid) and the base-pairs Adenine, Cytosine, Thymine, Guanine. The 6th is Uracil, which is used when DNA is transcribed to RNA. It replaces Thymine.<P>Now, the length of the DNA chain makes the DNA molecule VERY complex. But the reality is that all of it's components are very simple. This goes for most proteins. A protein is simply a combination of Amino acids, from an "alphabet" of 20 basic Amino Acids. Simple molecules. Amino acids can be formed easily, and if a couple interact in a certain way, you get an organic protein. This is how life is theorized to have started. A few naturally formed Amino acids met in a "tar pond" and formed the first basic organic protein. This started reacting with other amino acids, forming new compounds etc. Eventually, the proteins started working together, and formed a dicrete unit. Behold, the first organism. Life in this manner has been replicated in test-tubes. Going from a couple of molecules to people takes billions of years of trial-and-error recombination. DNA itself came a little later. You don't need DNA to live. Some viruses are only equiped with a primitive, very short version of RNA, which is simpler, and single-stranded. <BR>Here's the chemical composition of all the amino acids used in our particular lifeforms: <BR> <A HREF="http://prowl.rockefeller.edu/aainfo/struct.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://prowl.rockefeller.edu/aainfo/struct.htm</A> <BR>*notice that the carboxyl group is omitted. Simply tack on "NH2CHCOOH" to each of them.<BR>So you see, it's fairly easy to get organic reactions going. By that note, life should be fairly abundant. However, the steps to make a simple group of reactions evolve into a complex high-order thinking individual are fiendishly complex, and take forever to transpire. However, my argument is that due to the simplicity of the basic reactions necessary to life as WE know it, life should be plentiful throughout the universe. As to wether INTELLIGENT life exists, that remains to be seen.<P>As for the crop-circle thing, I've seen videos of 3 guys make an unbelievable crop-circle pattern. Scientists calculated that it was impossible to make in one evening, and impossible to do with any accuracy. 6 hours later, and the pattern was complete, and nearly perfect. Crop circles are made by bored college students. Come talk to me when you find one where the ground has been fused into glass, but the surrounding crop is untouched.<P>Game on!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
